diff --git a/specs/state.md b/specs/state.md
index 26bd108..2202366 100644
--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -577,6 +577,57 @@
   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+`RunState.result_persistence_profile` is an optional, additive field (schema stays `2.1`).
+Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence: `to_dict()` omits the key and
+`from_dict()` of a payload without it yields `None`. The only supported value is
+`derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the
+profile at `RunState` construction, at `StateManager.initialize(...)` and on load (a failed
+load leaves the state file byte-for-byte unchanged). Loads never infer, backfill or upgrade
+the field.
+
+**Selection.** `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the
+field with the initial state. A typed public `.orc` run and a new root created by
+`resume --force-restart` select the profile (the force-restart source run is not modified; the
+new root carries the requested observability settings). A fresh, non-iterative child call frame
+selects it when the callee bundle's validated provenance has `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"`;
+selection never reads the parent's profile, a path suffix, an alias or a step identity. Existing
+roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned frames keep the historical
+profile. An existing frame whose `state` is absent or not a mapping is rejected with a
+`ValueError` ("existing call-frame state") before anything is written;
+`load_existing_call_frame_read_only(frame)` returns a detached copy of that state.
+
+**Eligibility.** A compiler-generated `pure_projection` that is acyclic and visited at most
+once per scope is replay-eligible. Recurrent, loop-owned or otherwise multiply visited pure nodes
+keep full rows, bundles and checkpoints. `derive_pure_result_replay_index(bundle)` computes the
+eligible nodes, their typed binding addresses and dependency edges without mutating the bundle.
+
+**Durable shape.** An eligible success is persisted only as the exact completion shell
+`{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+"outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed",
+"retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}`. Failed and skipped rows stay
+full rows. Eligible nodes own no result bundle, no `private_artifact_versions` entry, no
+checkpoint record (their points are filtered before unique-nearest selection) and no restore
+binding. A persisted value row, bundle, lineage entry, checkpoint record or restore binding for an
+eligible node is a `profile_conflict` (`context.surface` is one of `steps`, `pure_bundle`,
+`private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record`, `restore_payload`) raised before the prologue.
+
+**Visits.** Each state transition is one atomic write: `begin_eligible_pure_visit` (visit count and
+`pure_projection` cursor), `settle_eligible_pure_success` (shell, cursor cleared) and
+`settle_eligible_pure_failure` (full row, cursor cleared). Progress classifies as `unstarted`,
+`interrupted`, `derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip` or `progress_witness_invalid`; a
+second visit is never valid.
+
+**Resume.** Resume re-derives the needed pure values in memory from validated durable leaves
+(bound inputs and durable dependency rows) and never dispatches an effect, increments a visit or
+writes state while doing so. Failures end the run with `error.type = pure_result_replay_unavailable`
+and `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`,
+`binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid` or `progress_witness_invalid`.
+Default resume admits exactly one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (mode
+`LEXICAL_CHECKPOINT_DEFAULT`, no checkpoint id, `selection_reason = validated_frame_entry_replay`),
+and otherwise fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
